	"responsive": {
		"strategy": "The whole page is one column at every width we shot, because it is built as one literal HTML `<table>` rather than any CSS layout system. The table holds 85% of the window's width and centres itself with an old `<center>` tag on a laptop, a desktop and an ultrawide screen alike, and there is no cap on that 85% at all — on the 3440 shot a comment thread stretches to nearly 3000px wide, which almost no modern site allows. Only on a phone-sized screen does the percentage rule stop: the table then fills the screen edge to edge with no side margin and no menu collapses into a hamburger, the links just stay put.",
