	"notes": "Hacker News looks the same at every size because it barely tries to be responsive: it is one long list of stories, built with an actual HTML table the way pages were built before CSS layout existed. On a laptop, a desktop monitor or an ultrawide screen it keeps the same shape and just gets wider, with no limit on how wide a line of text is allowed to get — most sites cap that around 600-800px so a sentence stays easy to read, but Hacker News does not. On a phone the table simply touches both edges of the screen instead of leaving margins. We could not pin the exact pixel width where that switch happens from the four shots alone, so the 600px breakpoint here is a best guess from the site's own CSS, not something we saw change on screen.",
